// Parcel's own pipeline, minus Babel (26.1004).
//
// Parcel compiles the site's JavaScript itself (@parcel/transformer-js, which
// is SWC). It only hands a file to Babel when it finds a Babel config FILE
// above it — and the one such file in src/ is the asteroids submodule's
// .babelrc. Parcel 2 can only drive Babel 7 (it asks for @babel/core ^7.12.0),
// and this repo's Babel is 8 now, used by jest alone. So the asteroids game
// would fail the build ("Could not find module @babel/core satisfying
// ^7.12.0"). Dropping Babel here compiles asteroids the same way as every
// other file on the site.
//
// ⚠️ The Dockerfile copies this file in by name: an image built without it
// falls back to Parcel's default pipeline and fails the same way.
{
  "extends": "@parcel/config-default",
  "transformers": {
    "*.{js,mjs,jsm,jsx,es6,cjs,ts,tsx}": [
      "@parcel/transformer-js",
      "@parcel/transformer-react-refresh-wrap"
    ]
  }
}
